      "role": "user",
      "content": "That sounds like a very convenient way to rebrand a collapse, but it doesn't hold up against the unit economics. If customers are just being \"more discerning,\" why is the basket size for this category also shrinking? \n\nI'm seeing a direct correlation between the lower conversion and a massive drop in the average order value for Neon Minimalism. If we commit to these high-volume orders and the conversion rate stays low while the value per customer keeps dropping, we aren't just \"maturing\"—we're bleeding margin. Can you point to any specific segment where the conversion or basket size is actually holding steady to prove this isn't a total exit from the trend?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
